  "note": "Hand-authored, self-contained, CROSS-PROJECT corpus for the Impact Analysis consumer recall/precision eval (#959, epic #954). Two small applications — a storefront (org.shop.*) and a reporting/batch app (com.report.*) — run over ONE physical database and SHARE the `account` and `orders` tables (each app has its own private table too: `cart`, `report_run`). Each labeled requirement originates in the storefront and expects the reporting app to be flagged as a shared-table CONSUMER (expectedConsumers), alongside the affected tables. The graph is deliberately small and UN-polluted (mapper-only, no cross-layer service fan-out) so it isolates the cross-project signal — corpus-01 already measures single-project seed pollution. No DB, no network, no live LLM. HONEST BASELINE (pre-#955/#956, before the cross-project consumer wiring lands): the engine does not surface consumers, so consumer recall is 0.00 and precision is a VACUOUS 1.00 (nothing surfaced). This is the yardstick that makes #955/#956's lift visible; see README.md.",
